                <pb facs="0530" n="428" sameAs="frus:frus1927v03/pg428"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.51/1739: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Eberhardt</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-03-03T09:00:00-05:45"><hi rendition="#italic">March 3, 1927—9
                                a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 11:35 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>66. Diaz government, desperately in need of funds, will today make still another
                    effort to secure loan for which Diaz will offer bankers all stock in railway and
                    bank and lien against all revenue produced by recent law. It is hoped that the
                    terms may be such that the Department can and will approve. Otherwise Diaz sees
                    no alternative but an emergency emission of cordobas which sound bankers unite
                    in declaring will result in inflation and disaster to Nicaraguan finances.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Eberhardt</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
